WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.181
Meet Dana. Three weeks ago she was the best cook on the line at a campus dining hall.

2
00:00:07.231 --> 00:00:14.216
Now she runs it. And in her first week, she is still on the line, plating faster than anyone,

3
00:00:14.266 --> 00:00:18.226
while her team waits for decisions only she can make.

4
00:00:18.276 --> 00:00:23.295
That is the change nobody explains. Before, your job was your work.

5
00:00:23.345 --> 00:00:27.759
Now your job is your team’s work, and the people who do it.

6
00:00:27.809 --> 00:00:34.946
Three things are new for Dana. She decides: what matters this shift, who does what, what waits.

7
00:00:34.996 --> 00:00:41.376
She approves: timecards, time off, the schedule, and Vanderbilt trusts her signature,

8
00:00:41.426 --> 00:00:43.646
so she looks before she signs.

9
00:00:43.696 --> 00:00:50.757
And she is responsible for people: fair treatment, a safe place to speak up, a chance to grow.

10
00:00:50.807 --> 00:00:54.767
Watch what changes when she steps back from the line.

11
00:00:54.817 --> 00:00:58.172
She names the three things that matter today.

12
00:00:58.222 --> 00:01:05.283
She signs the timecards at the pass. She hears out a dishwasher who has something on his mind.

13
00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:09.444
Lunch runs better, and she did not plate a single tray.

14
00:01:09.494 --> 00:01:12.319
Dana does not have to know everything.

15
00:01:12.369 --> 00:01:18.069
She has an HCM, an Engagement Consultant, and a micro module for every task.

16
00:01:18.119 --> 00:01:21.473
What she has to do is show up as the manager.

17
00:01:21.523 --> 00:01:26.088
This week: notice the moment you want to just do it yourself.

18
00:01:26.138 --> 00:01:28.887
That is the moment to manage instead.

